@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";

    @* Kept in step with the Terms: registration stores ONE version against the account and
       it covers both documents. See LegalDocuments.Version. *@
    var version = LegalDocuments.Version;
    var termsUrl = Url.Action("Terms", "Home") ?? "/Home/Terms";

    @* SECTION 9 NAMES THE HOSTING PROVIDER AND ITS COUNTRY. If this application is deployed
       anywhere other than Azure App Service in North Europe (Ireland), section 9.3 and the
       transfers statement in section 10 are FALSE and must be corrected before the site is
       reachable. A privacy policy that names the wrong country is not a small error. *@
}

<div class="row justify-content-center">
    <div class="col-lg-9">
        <h1 class="h3 mb-1">Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="text-muted">
            Version: @version · Last updated: 16 September 2026
        </p>

        <p class="small text-muted">
            Published in English. Albanian and Italian versions are being prepared.
        </p>

        <p>
            This policy explains what PremiumMotors does with personal data. It is written to
            match what the software actually does. Where something is not built yet, it says so.
        </p>

        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">1. Who controls your data</h2>
        <p>
            <strong>Denis Robi</strong> is the data controller.<br />
            Contact for any privacy question or request:
            <a href="mailto:drobi840@gmail.com">drobi840@gmail.com</a>
        </p>
        <p>
            No Data Protection Officer has been appointed. At this scale one is not required:
            we are not a public body, and our core activity is not large-scale monitoring or
            large-scale processing of special-category data.
        </p>

        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">2. What we collect</h2>

        <h3 class="h6 mt-3">2.1 Account</h3>
        <p>
            Username, email address, telephone number, password, account role, whether the
            account is active, registration date, last login, and email-verification date.
        </p>
        <p>
            <strong>Passwords are never stored in readable form.</strong> They are hashed with
            PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA256 using a unique salt per account and 210,000 iterations.
        </p>

        <h3 class="h6 mt-3">2.2 Acceptance and erasure records</h3>
        <p>
            The date you accepted the Terms and which version you accepted; and, if your
            account is ever erased, the date that was carried out. These are kept as
            accountability records — being able to show that a request was acted on is part of
            having acted on it.
        </p>

        <h3 class="h6 mt-3">2.3 Seller profile</h3>
        <p>
            Whether the account sells, the date selling was enabled, private or dealer, display
            name, town or region, profile picture, rating average and rating count.
        </p>

        <h3 class="h6 mt-3">2.4 Optional public telephone number</h3>
        <p>
            A seller may choose to publish a telephone number. If set, <strong>it appears on
            every listing that seller owns and is visible to visitors who are not signed
            in.</strong> It is optional, it starts empty, and clearing it removes it from the
            site. Because it sits on a public page, it may be copied, indexed or scraped;
            removing it here does not remove copies others have already taken.
        </p>
        <p>
            This is deliberately separate from the telephone number on your account, which
            stays private until you accept or make an offer (section 5.3).
        </p>

        <h3 class="h6 mt-3">2.5 Business accounts</h3>
        <p>
            Business registration number (NIPT), VAT number, trading address, website and
            contact person. <strong>We do not check these against any register and there is no
            verified badge on this site for anyone.</strong>
        </p>

        <h3 class="h6 mt-3">2.6 Dealership page</h3>
        <p>
            Name, page address, about text, logo, banner, city, country, address, telephone,
            website and opening hours. All of it is public.
        </p>

        <h3 class="h6 mt-3">2.7 Listings</h3>
        <p>
            Everything the seller enters: vehicle details and specification, description,
            asking price, photographs, location, and after a sale the buyer, the agreed price
            and the date. A vehicle identification number (VIN), if the seller records one, is
            <strong>stored but never published</strong>.
        </p>

        <h3 class="h6 mt-3">2.8 Offers</h3>
        <p>
            Buyer, amount, the buyer's optional message, status, timestamps and the seller's
            written response. <strong>Offers are private to the seller who received them.</strong>
        </p>

        <h3 class="h6 mt-3">2.9 Messages</h3>
        <p>
            The full text of buyer–seller conversations, with the listing, sender and read
            time. Administrators can access message threads where necessary to operate, secure
            or support the service, or to deal with a report.
        </p>

        <h3 class="h6 mt-3">2.10 Reviews</h3>
        <p>
            Rating, comment, the reviewer's username, the listing, timestamps and the seller's
            public reply. Reviews are public. A review is only possible where the listing sold,
            the reviewer is the recorded buyer, and one review per sale. Removal is covered by
            section 16 of the <a href="@termsUrl">Terms</a>.
        </p>

        <h3 class="h6 mt-3">2.11 Favourites, price history, view counts</h3>
        <p>
            Saved listings. Every price change on a listing, with the date — parts of which are
            shown publicly as price-drop indicators. Listing views counted
            <strong>in aggregate, per listing per day</strong>: we do not record who viewed a
            listing. A browser session is used to avoid counting the same visit twice, and the
            seller's own views are excluded.
        </p>

        <h3 class="h6 mt-3">2.12 Sessions and tokens</h3>
        <p>
            Server-side session state, held in our database and linked to an opaque cookie. It
            may contain your user ID, username, seller or administrator flags, recently viewed
            listing IDs and the markers used to avoid double-counting views.
        </p>
        <p>
            For the mobile and API login, refresh-token records hold a
            <strong>hash</strong> of the token, its creation, expiry and revocation times, and
            a device label taken from the browser or app. Email-verification and password-reset
            records hold a hash, the purpose, expiry and when it was used.
            <strong>The token values themselves are never stored.</strong>
        </p>

        <h3 class="h6 mt-3">2.13 Logs and IP addresses</h3>
        <p>
            Application logs record the request method, path, response status and how long it
            took. <strong>They do not record IP addresses.</strong>
        </p>
        <p>
            For requests from visitors who are not signed in, an IP address is used in memory
            as the key for rate limiting and is not stored by the application. Our hosting
            provider may record IP addresses independently in its own infrastructure logs.
        </p>

        <h3 class="h6 mt-3">2.14 Advertising records</h3>
        <p>
            Where a paid placement is granted we keep a receipt: a reference code, the listing
            title as it read at the time, the placement type, start and end dates, who granted
            it and any price. These records survive the end of the placement and the deletion
            of the listing, because they are transaction records.
        </p>

        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">3. What we do not collect</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>No card or bank details. There is no payment processor connected to this site.</li>
            <li>No identity documents and no date of birth.</li>
            <li>No advertising or analytics trackers, and no third-party cookies.</li>
            <li>No cross-site tracking and no fingerprinting.</li>
            <li>No location data beyond the town a user types in.</li>
            <li>No scripts, fonts or stylesheets loaded from anyone else's domain — everything
                the site serves comes from the site itself.</li>
            <li>No special-category data.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-muted small">
            If any of this changes, this section changes before the new technology goes live.
        </p>

        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">4. Why we process it, and on what basis</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>To perform our contract with you</strong> — creating and running your
                account, publishing your listings, delivering offers and messages, running
                favourites, dealership pages and reviews.</li>
            <li><strong>Our legitimate interests</strong> — keeping the service secure,
                preventing fraud and abuse, rate limiting, troubleshooting, publishing sold
                prices and sold history so the marketplace is useful to buyers, and giving
                sellers view and offer statistics about their own listings.</li>
            <li><strong>Legal obligation and accountability</strong> — keeping records of
                terms acceptance, of erasure requests, and of advertising transactions.</li>
            <li><strong>Consent</strong> — only where we ask for it. We do not send marketing
                email, and we would not do so without asking first.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">5. What other people can see</h2>

        <h3 class="h6 mt-3">5.1 Public to anyone, including signed-out visitors</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>Seller display name, or username where no display name is set</li>
            <li>Whether the seller is private or a dealership</li>
            <li>Profile photograph, dealership logo and banner</li>
            <li>Rating average and review count</li>
            <li>Reviews, their text, and each reviewer's username</li>
            <li>The public telephone number, if the seller chose to publish one</li>
            <li>Dealership name, address, telephone, website, opening hours and about text</li>
            <li>Listings, photographs, specification and asking price</li>
            <li>Price-change history and price-drop indicators</li>
            <li><strong>Completed sales and the agreed sale price</strong>, for 14 days</li>
            <li>Whether a listing is a paid placement</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
            Anything public can be indexed by search engines and copied by third parties.
        </p>

        <h3 class="h6 mt-3">5.2 Private</h3>
        <p>
            Offer amounts and offer messages are visible only to the seller who received them,
            and to administrators. Conversations are visible to their participants, and to
            administrators where necessary. VINs, business registration and VAT numbers,
            trading addresses and contact-person names are not published.
        </p>

        <h3 class="h6 mt-3">5.3 Contact details when an offer is accepted</h3>
        <p>
            <strong>When a seller accepts an offer, the buyer and the seller each receive the
            other's email address and telephone number</strong> so they can arrange the sale.
            This is a disclosure of your personal data to another user, triggered by an action
            one of you takes. Declined and withdrawn offers release nothing.
        </p>

        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">6. Published sale prices</h2>
        <p>
            When a sale completes we publish the agreed price on the Recently sold page. The
            seller is told this on the screen where they accept the offer, not only here.
        </p>
        <p>
            That page shows the last 14 days. <strong>The 14 days is a display rule, not a
            deletion rule</strong> — older sales stop appearing there but the record, the price
            and the price history are kept.
        </p>

        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">7. Cookies and browser storage</h2>
        <p>Only essential storage is used. There are three cookies and one browser flag.</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Session cookie</strong> — an opaque identifier for your server-side
                session. HttpOnly, SameSite=Lax, Secure over HTTPS, and it expires after about
                two hours of inactivity.</li>
            <li><strong>Anti-forgery cookie</strong> — protects forms against cross-site
                request forgery.</li>
            <li><strong>Language cookie</strong> — set only when you choose a language from the
                picker. It holds a language code, lasts about a year, and is readable by the
                page, which is why it is not HttpOnly.</li>
            <li><strong>Browser sessionStorage</strong> — one flag, so the arrival animation
                runs once per browser session. It stays in your browser and is never sent to us.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
            <strong>No analytics cookie, no advertising cookie, no third-party cookie, no
            fingerprinting.</strong> That is why this site has no cookie banner: there is
            nothing here to consent to beyond what is strictly necessary to make it work.
        </p>

        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">8. Who else processes your data</h2>
        <p>
            <strong>Supabase</strong> — hosts our PostgreSQL database and stores uploaded
            photographs. Region: <strong>West EU (Ireland)</strong>.
        </p>
        <p>
            <strong>Microsoft Azure App Service</strong> — hosts the application itself.
            Region: <strong>North Europe (Ireland)</strong>. The hosting infrastructure may
            record IP addresses and technical request information in its own logs.
        </p>
        <p>
            <strong>Resend</strong> — would send verification and password-reset email.
            <strong>Email is not switched on. No email provider is configured, so no email is
            being sent to anyone and Resend currently receives no data about you.</strong> This
            section will be updated before that changes.
        </p>
        <p>
            <strong>Sentry</strong> — error monitoring. It is present in the code but
            <strong>inactive</strong>: with no key configured it makes no network calls. If it
            is ever switched on, it is configured not to send personal data or request bodies.
        </p>
        <p>
            That is the complete list. <strong>No payment processor, no analytics provider, no
            advertising network, no data broker.</strong>
        </p>

        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">9. International transfers</h2>
        <p>
            Our database, our file storage and our application hosting are all located in
            <strong>Ireland, inside the European Economic Area</strong>. We do not transfer
            your personal data outside the EEA.
        </p>

        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">10. How long we keep it</h2>
        <p>
            We do not run a general automatic deletion schedule, and we would rather say so
            than publish a number the software does not enforce. What actually happens:
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Account and profile data</strong> — until you ask us to erase it.</li>
            <li><strong>Listings, offers, messages, reviews, favourites and price history</strong>
                — kept while the account exists, and subject to erasure as described in
                section 11.</li>
            <li><strong>Completed sales</strong> — kept indefinitely as transaction records.
                Displayed on Recently sold for 14 days.</li>
            <li><strong>Web sessions</strong> — two hours of inactivity, then removed
                automatically.</li>
            <li><strong>Refresh tokens</strong> — 30 days, and revoked immediately when you
                change your password.</li>
            <li><strong>Verification and password-reset tokens</strong> — until they expire or
                are used.</li>
            <li><strong>Application logs</strong> — 14 days, then overwritten.</li>
            <li><strong>Advertising records</strong> — kept as long as accounting and tax rules
                require.</li>
            <li><strong>Terms acceptance and erasure timestamps</strong> — kept after
                anonymisation, because they are the record that we acted correctly.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">11. Erasing your account</h2>
        <p>
            You can erase your account yourself from the <a href="@Url.Action("Security", "Account")">Security</a> page of your profile,
            which asks for your password again to confirm it is you. If you cannot sign in, email
            <a href="mailto:drobi840@gmail.com">drobi840@gmail.com</a> instead. Being straight
            about what erasure means:
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li>Your username, email, telephone number and public telephone number are cleared,
                and you are signed out on every device.</li>
            <li>Dealership name, about text, address, telephone, website and opening hours are
                blanked.</li>
            <li><strong>Every image you uploaded is deleted</strong> — profile picture,
                dealership logo and banner, and the photographs on every listing you posted.</li>
            <li><strong>Completed sales remain</strong> on the sold history, without
                photographs and without identifying you, labelled "Dealership closed". A sale
                that happened is a record the other party has a legitimate interest in.</li>
            <li>Reviews you wrote about other sellers, and messages you sent, remain under an
                anonymous name - never your own - so that a seller's rating cannot be rewritten by
                a departing buyer, and the other side of a conversation still makes sense.</li>
            <li>We record the date the erasure was carried out.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
            The right to erasure is subject to the exceptions the law allows, including where
            we need to keep something to establish, exercise or defend a legal claim.
        </p>

        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">12. Getting a copy of your data</h2>
        <p>
            Download it yourself from the <a href="@Url.Action("Security", "Account")">Security</a> page of your profile: one file, in a
            common machine-readable format, available immediately. You can also ask by email.
        </p>
        <p>
            It contains your account and sign-in history, your terms acceptance, your seller,
            business and dealership details, your listings and their price history, offers you
            made and offers made on your listings, your conversations and messages, reviews you
            wrote and reviews written about you, your favourites, and any advertising records.
            Other people's contact details are not included.
        </p>

        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">13. Your rights</h2>
        <p>Subject to the conditions in the law, you have the right to:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>access your personal data;</li>
            <li>have inaccurate or incomplete data corrected;</li>
            <li>have your data erased in the circumstances the law allows;</li>
            <li>restrict or object to processing in some circumstances;</li>
            <li>receive your data in a portable form;</li>
            <li>withdraw consent, where we relied on consent; and</li>
            <li>complain to the supervisory authority.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
            Much of this you can do yourself: your email and telephone number are editable on
            your profile, and your listings and dealership page are editable at any time. For
            anything else, email
            <a href="mailto:drobi840@gmail.com">drobi840@gmail.com</a>.
            Downloading your data and erasing your account can both be done immediately from
            the <a href="@Url.Action("Security", "Account")">Security</a> page. Emailed requests are answered within one month.
        </p>
        <p>
            We may need to confirm who you are before acting on a request.
        </p>

        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">14. Complaining to the regulator</h2>
        <p>
            You can complain to the Albanian supervisory authority, the
            <strong>Commissioner for the Right to Information and Protection of Personal
            Data</strong> — <a href="https://idp.al/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">idp.al</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
            If you are in the European Union you may also complain to the supervisory authority
            in your own country.
        </p>

        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">15. Security</h2>
        <p>We use measures appropriate to what we hold, including:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>passwords hashed, never stored readably;</li>
            <li>refresh, verification and reset tokens stored only as hashes;</li>
            <li>session state kept on the server, not in the browser;</li>
            <li>HttpOnly, Secure and SameSite controls on cookies;</li>
            <li>anti-forgery protection on forms;</li>
            <li>rate limiting; and</li>
            <li>administrative access restricted to accounts that need it.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
            No online service can promise absolute security, and we are not going to pretend
            otherwise.
        </p>

        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">16. Data breaches</h2>
        <p>
            If a personal-data breach happens we will assess it and notify the supervisory
            authority and, where the law requires, the people affected, within the time limits
            the law sets.
        </p>

        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">17. Age</h2>
        <p>
            This site is for people aged <strong>18 or over</strong>. We do not knowingly
            collect data about anyone younger. We do not verify age at registration; if we
            learn that an account belongs to someone under 18 we will close it and delete the
            data.
        </p>

        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">18. Automated decisions</h2>
        <p>
            We do not make decisions about you by automated means alone, and we do not profile
            you.
        </p>

        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">19. Business users</h2>
        <p>
            Dealership accounts are responsible for the accuracy of their own business
            information and for their own obligations as traders — listings, consumer sales,
            advertising, invoicing, taxation and guarantees.
        </p>

        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">20. Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>
            We update this policy when the service, the technology or the law changes. The
            version number here is the same one recorded against your account when you
            registered, and the two are always changed together. Where a change is material we
            will notify you.
        </p>

        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">21. Contact</h2>
        <p>
            Denis Robi<br />
            <a href="mailto:drobi840@gmail.com">drobi840@gmail.com</a>
        </p>
    </div>
</div>
